From 1bc72eb9f2a86cbd8770b5f95f60e71837f5b284 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Laksh Goyal <laksh.g@gmicloud.ai>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 02:42:59 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] vmm: add DiffLive snapshot type for live migration pre-copy

Firecracker snapshots require paused vCPUs because the vCPU/device state
save is only valid when stopped. The guest-memory dump has no such
requirement, so this adds SnapshotType::DiffLive: a diff snapshot that dumps
dirty guest memory while the vCPUs keep running, skipping the state save
entirely (a live-migration pre-copy round).

Correctness rests on two properties. Guest writes racing the dump are
handled by KVM's fetch-and-clear dirty log: a racing write is either in the
bitmap already fetched (its page is dumped, possibly torn) or in KVM's fresh
bitmap (re-dumped next round), so torn pages are always re-marked dirty.
VMM-side writes (virtio) cannot race the dump because device emulation runs
on the same thread. A live dump therefore preserves the VMM-internal dirty
bitmap rather than resetting it; only a final paused Diff resets.

To bound how long one call occupies the VMM event loop (which also services
virtio), live_max_bytes caps the dump. Over-budget dirty pages are recorded
back into the VMM dirty bitmap, which then acts as the drain backlog: each
subsequent round fetches KVM's log again, ORs in that backlog, ships another
budget's worth, and re-records the rest, so the residual shrinks whenever the
guest dirties less than a budget per round. dirty_backlog_bytes() exposes the
backlog size for observability.

Adds unit tests for the drain, the budget split, and backlog accounting;
swagger and API metrics updated. No change to Full or Diff behavior.
